From 443c92fa40384a9a3853b417de2b6d4e3ce92383 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vatte Vishnuvardhan Reddy <vishnuvr@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 14:24:21 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phy: aquantia: Fix aqr_set_rxsc using get instead of set
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

aqr_set_rxsc() builds the ingress SC record (validate_frames, valid,
fresh) then calls aqr_mss_get_ingress_sc_record() which reads from
hardware and discards the built record. Should call
aqr_mss_set_ingress_sc_record() to write it.

Effect: ingress SC never programmed into PHY → all RX MACsec frames
hit InPktsNoSCI counter → zero decryption.

Change-Id: Ic87877b1e4656adb02b6e85a0a10431efbacdd1b
Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Vatte Vishnuvardhan Reddy <vishnuvr@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 macsec/macsec.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/macsec/macsec.c b/macsec/macsec.c
index 5405988..d4843d7 100644
--- a/macsec/macsec.c
+++ b/macsec/macsec.c
@@ -801,7 +801,7 @@ static int aqr_set_rxsc(struct aqr107_priv *priv, const u32 rxsc_idx)
 	sc_record.valid = 1;
 	sc_record.fresh = 1;

-	ret = aqr_mss_get_ingress_sc_record(port, &sc_record, hw_sc_idx);
+	ret = aqr_mss_set_ingress_sc_record(port, &sc_record, hw_sc_idx);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;

--
2.34.1

